The Sword Saint is the neutral elite of the Kensai. It is the duelist's end:
Focus builds higher, Iaijutsu hits harder and more surely, and at the top rank
the first draw is followed by a second.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

  30 Still mind         Focus builds +5% for each quiet round, up to +25%
  35 Perfect cut        +4 Attack
  40 Piercing sight     Iaijutsu's critical chance is +20%
  45 Lingering Zanshin  Zanshin gives three quarters of a turn
  50 Deeper edge        Iaijutsu deals 100% more damage
  55 Saint's eye        +4% critical chance
  60 Twin draw          Iaijutsu carries the edge of its first two strikes of
                        a battle

It needs the Kensai first (<ansi fg="command">help samurai-routes</ansi>) and keeps every rank of it. At level 30 a
character that holds it promotes with <ansi fg="command">class promote [member] sword-saint confirm</ansi>. Any alignment may take it.
Everything here lasts only for the battle and is never saved.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

Elite Samurai talents (levels 35, 45, 55): Razor's Edge (+5% critical chance
on every blow), Quick Hands (starts a battle with 15 points on its action
meter), Shadow Footing (+5 Evasion). See <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help samurai-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.
